  "ui_tests_run": false,
  "changes": [
    "Checkbox values and switch checked/slide/hover transition data now live in optional boxed NodeModel payloads of Rust ActionNodeRecord. Native adapters keep only their ActionControl lease, not separately owned CheckboxState or ToggleState boxes. Ordinary action records do not allocate a typed payload.",
    "Typed binding is explicit and idempotent for the same kind, preserving existing values on adapter replacement. Wrong-kind binding, standalone/unbound input, stale leases and retired scopes reject model access. Dropping an adapter detaches input but leaves the logical node model in the graph; retiring the node or dropping the graph releases its payload immediately even if old adapters still retain their input record.",
    "User flips require both current graph input enablement and native admission. Backend value projection remains allowed while input is disabled, preserving managed/disabled UI refresh semantics. Native browser/pref/import validation and callbacks remain authoritative.",
    "Switch render state uses NodeToggleView (checked/progress/hover/animating) read from one record at one timestamp. Existing transition durations, interruption/backwards-clock policy and finish semantics delegate to the established reducers. Timers and native Metal/window/AX adapters remain; no end-to-end speedup is claimed.",
    "Old checkbox/switch constructors and type handles were removed from the C++ bridge. The standalone reducer constructors now exist only in Rust tests for oracle checks. This prevents the actual native controls from constructing independently owned typed models.",
    "Eight new Rust tests cover adapter drop/rebinding, type/lease/standalone rejection, enabled user mutation versus disabled projection, payload release, legacy animation parity, sibling/failed-reconciliation isolation and finish/retirement. Two compiled-only browser cases cover actual model kinds/projections and checked-state-before-observer ordering, retirement and adapter survival through controller teardown."
  ],
  "deferred_gui_cases": [
    "ZitterProfilesBrowserTest.CheckedModelsBelongToNodesAcrossProjectionAndDisabledRefresh",
    "ZitterProfilesBrowserTest.CheckedModelRetiresDuringObserverBeforeImportCallback",
    "ZitterProfilesBrowserTest.CheckedActionHostsAXAndViewportCancellation",
    "ZitterProfilesBrowserTest.CheckedAndSelectorNodesCoverLiveFormsAndRetainProjectionIdentity",
